/bench/tables/cs/obj/
# a `go build` in bench/go drops the leg's binary beside its source
/bench/go/benchgo

# bench-local scratch/verification debris — never repo content
tending/

# CI clones the five serialize runtimes here (see .github/workflows/ci.yml)
/runtimes/

# a `go build ./bench/tools/...` run from the repository root drops its binary
# at ./tools, and one reached main once already (#32). The ignore is for THAT
# FILE. The negation re-includes the DIRECTORY of the same name, which carries
# tracked tool sources the build runs (tools/sabotage, the wide-text negative
# controls): a trailing slash matches only a directory, so the stray binary
# stays ignored and the sources stay committable.
/tools
!/tools/

# test-leg build artifact
/test/go/schematest

# pinned toolchains unpacked locally (Dart SDK, JDK — see the Makefile DART and JAVA variables)
/dist

# a crashed BEAM run drops its dump wherever it ran
erl_crash.dump
/schema

# the Go table gates leave a test binary behind when `go test` is run with a
# profile flag; it is a build artifact and never a source
/test/go-tables/schematables.test

# `go build ./test/conformance/harness` run from the repository root drops the
# binary here rather than in build/ — the Makefile always names `-o` and never
# wants this file. It reached main once already (#345).
/harness
